# Known Issues

This file tracks known bugs, limitations, and deferred work items for the project.

## How to Use

- **Before working on a component**: Check this file for known problems
  that may affect your work or that your work could address.
- **When discovering a new issue**: Add an entry with status, date, component,
  problem description, and any known root cause or workaround.
- **When resolving an issue**: Update the status to "Resolved" with the date and
  a brief note on the fix, but keep the entry for historical context.

## Current Open Issues

- **ML Table Detection underperforms heuristic** -- `MLTableDetection/TableDetectorML.py`
  exists and has been trained through four iterations (v2, v4, v5, v5b). The best model
  (v4) achieves mAP@0.5 of 0.66 on `generic3.pdf` but still trails the heuristic
  `PanelSearchToolV25` which finds all 6 panels. Adding negative examples (v5, v5b)
  caused regressions. v4 remains the best Table Transformer model.
  **Root cause identified (2026-05-06)**: dataset size is the primary bottleneck.
  Microsoft Table Transformer maintainers recommend ~1,000 images as the
  fine-tuning floor (per [microsoft/table-transformer Issue #108](https://github.com/microsoft/table-transformer/issues/108));
  the original `annotations_coco.json` had only 28 images with annotations.
  See "Dataset expansion (Phase 1) -- DONE" entry below for the v6 dataset and
  remaining Phase 2 audit gaps in `train_table_transformer.py`.

- **Dataset expansion (Phase 1) -- DONE 2026-05-06** -- A 298-image / 821-annotation
  training dataset has been built at `~/Documents/TableAnnotations/v6/` from
  the original 48 real images plus 250 synthetic images generated via
  cut-and-paste augmentation ([Dwibedi et al. 2017](https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.01642)).
  Scripts created:
  - `MLTableDetection/pseudo_label.py` -- TATR v4 + threshold router
    (auto-accept / review / hard-negatives) for any future rendered pages.
    Run on 49 rendered PDF pages: 0 auto-accepted, 3 routed to review,
    46 already in original COCO so skipped.
  - `MLTableDetection/synthesize_panels.py` -- generates synthetic pages by
    white-masking original panel regions and compositing real panel crops
    onto natural-blank or masked backgrounds with small affine and
    photometric variations.
  - `MLTableDetection/merge_annotations.py` -- multi-source COCO merger
    that re-keys IDs, hardlinks images, and tracks per-image source role.
  Important caveats:
    - Synthetic dominates the dataset (84%); held-out validation should
      be drawn from real images only.
    - 298 is still below Microsoft's ~1,000-image floor; further gains
      may require collecting more real PDFs.
    - 3 review-pile images at `~/Documents/TableAnnotations/pseudo_labeling/review/`
      (B_page001.png, derek2_page009.png, derekfirst_page007.png) need manual
      annotation if you want to add them to the v6 dataset.

- **Phase 2 audit gaps in `train_table_transformer.py`** -- The training script
  has correct augmentation, train/val split, and mAP tracking, but is missing
  three documented small-dataset levers:
  1. `--num-queries` is not exposed (uses TATR default 15). Per
     [DETR Issue #9](https://github.com/facebookresearch/detr/issues/9) and
     [Issue #620](https://github.com/facebookresearch/detr/issues/620) it
     should be set modestly above the max objects per image (panels max ~6,
     suggested value 15-20).
  2. `--freeze-backbone-epochs` flag missing. With small datasets,
     [Dynamic Backbone Freezing (arxiv 2407.15143)](https://arxiv.org/html/2407.15143v4)
     recommends freezing the backbone for the first 30% of training epochs.
  3. No targeted-negatives mode. v5/v5b regressed because random negatives
     were added at image level rather than as targeted false-positive crops.
     Phase 2 should add a separate hard-negatives folder weighted lower in the loss.
  Plan reference: `~/.cursor/plans/panel-detector-improvement-path_9fdbc9ca.plan.md`.

- **ML Page Classifier created** -- `PageFilter/PageClassifierML.py` provides a
  MobileNetV2 binary classifier for page-level "has panel / no panel" decisions.
  Trained on 35 images (28 pos, 7 neg), achieves 100% val accuracy. Designed as
  a faster drop-in replacement for the heuristic page filter (~250 ms/page vs
  ~1-3 s). Wrapped by `PageFilter/PageFilterV4.py`, which exposes the same
  `PageFilter` class and `readPdf()` signature as earlier heuristic versions
  for transparent swap-in. Not yet integrated into `uplink_server.py` (still
  imports `PageFilterV3`).

- **uplink_server.py imports PageFilterV3** -- V3 is the last heuristic page
  filter; V4 is an ML-based wrapper around `PageClassifierML` (MobileNetV2).
  `uplink_server.py` still imports `PageFilter.PageFilterV3` and has not yet
  been switched to V4.
